# 🟠 Level 3 – Broken Access Control

# What is Access Control?

Access Control determines:

Who can access

What resource

Under which conditions.

---

# Broken Access Control

Occurs when users gain access to resources they should **not** be able to access.

---

Example

Admin Dashboard

↓

Normal User

↓

Access Granted ❌

This is Broken Access Control.

---

# Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR)

IDOR occurs when an application exposes a reference to an object (such as a record ID) but **fails to verify that the user is authorized** to access that object.

---

## Example

Suppose your profile URL is:

```text
/profile?id=105
```

The server should verify:

> Is the logged-in user allowed to access profile 105?

If the server only checks the number and not the user's permissions,

another user's data could become accessible.

---

# Why IDOR Happens

Developers:

❌ Check only whether the user is logged in.

But forget to check:

✔ Whether the user is authorized for that specific resource.

---

# RBAC (Role-Based Access Control)

Users receive permissions based on roles.

Example:

```text
Admin

↓

Create Users

Delete Users

Manage Servers

↓

Employee

↓

View Own Profile

Update Own Password
```

---

# Least Privilege

Every user receives only the permissions necessary.

Intern

↓

Read Documents

Not

↓

Delete Database

---

# 🌍 Real-World Example

A university portal.

Student A logs in.

The server verifies:

Student ID = 105.

If Student A attempts to request another student's record,

the application should check ownership before returning any information.

Proper authorization prevents unauthorized access.

---

# Secure Authorization Checklist

✔ Verify permissions on every request.

✔ Never trust hidden form fields.

✔ Never trust URL parameters alone.

✔ Perform server-side authorization checks.

✔ Use RBAC.

✔ Log authorization failures.

---

# 🧠 Common Beginner Mistakes

❌ Believing login automatically means permission.

❌ Performing authorization only in the frontend.

❌ Giving every employee administrator rights.

❌ Forgetting ownership checks.

